<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Priarius</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 378</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Priarius was king of the Alemannic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lentienses">Lentienses</a>. In early 378, learning that much of the Western Roman army had been sent east, his people crossed the frozen <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a> into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alsace">Alsace</a>, but they were defeated by Gratian's generals <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nannienus">Nannienus</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mallobaudes">Mallobaudes</a> at Argentovaria. Priarius, described by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ammianus-marcellinus">Ammianus Marcellinus</a> as the instigator of the attack, was killed in the battle.</p></div>
